# Wave W17-AA (Route 221): ring post — a tide-ring marker post at the rock-ringed pools: a weathered post with a ring of small pale stones laid at its foot, marking the pools that keep their tiny worlds (design: rock-ringed tide pools along the shore — the rings are the coast’s own punctuation, the posts stand where the pools begin). On tide turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s marker posts by the ring entire: posts mark a road, this one marks a pool’s edge.
